From 39d20f223ec1e063771a5c172312f57b03ca9a44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:25:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/31] Fold the GDN conv-state shuffle into the ssm_conv

Each gated delta net layer rolled its conv state with four launches before the
conv: GET_ROWS (cache row -> state), CONCAT (state | new columns), CPY (the
last columns back into the cache, one per rollback snapshot) and SSM_CONV.
For one sequence and up to 8 new tokens (decode and MTP verify) a single
kernel now does all of it: each thread owns a channel, keeps its old state in
registers, writes the state updates, then runs the conv with the same loads
and sums as ssm_conv_f32, so the result is bit-exact.

The matcher (ggml_cuda_p60_conv_state_plan) checks the whole run at the gather
and records it; the gather, concat and copies are then skipped and the conv
node launches the fused kernel. It needs nothing but views and those copies
between the concat and the conv, otherwise the new columns' buffer could be
reused before the conv reads it, so qwen35moe now expands the conv and silu
right after the conv-state update (node order only). Only on with
GGML_CUDA_P60_MMVQ=1; GGML_CUDA_P60_FUSE_CONV_STATE=0 turns it off.

2x P100: about 120 launches/token fewer, decode wall 15.50 -> 15.07 ms/token
in the trace, MTP 8-prompt 110.9 -> 112.7 t/s (+1.6%, two rounds, same
acceptance). Wikitext KLD at ub=1 vs the previous commit: 0, same top 100%,
ub=4 identical; MTP outputs byte-identical.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
